<template><main class="about-page"><AppHeader/><article class="prose"><h1>Local-only by design</h1><p class="lead">Your maps stay in this browser.</p><section class="privacy-card"><strong>About & privacy</strong><p>Mapworks has no account, backend, cloud sync, telemetry, or error reporting. When you deliberately use a WebMCP read tool, the bounded map data returned by that tool is shared with the browser agent you chose.</p></section><h2>What stays on your device</h2><p>Maps, tile chunks, structures, objects, labels, layers, and preferences live in IndexedDB in this browser. Mapworks never auto-purges your work.</p><h2>Portable by design</h2><p>Export a complete <code>.mapworks</code> archive whenever you like. You can also export a PNG for players or a Markdown map key for your notes.</p><h2>Browser-agent collaboration</h2><p>In a compatible browser, WebMCP lets an agent paint regions, construct rooms, draw walls, and place semantic objects through bounded bulk tools. Changes are visible and saved locally before a tool reports success. Removing map elements requires your approval.</p><RouterLink class="button primary" to="/">All maps</RouterLink></article></main></template>
